    "literal_raw_utf8": "{\"mathdb_id\": 375537, \"uuid\": \"6c8f862e-191b-40bd-91e2-2c73122ddf2b\", \"canonical_url\": \"https://mathdb.com/p/375537/esperet-et-al-s-flow-reconfiguration-equivalence-conjecture\", \"title\": \"Esperet et al.'s flow reconfiguration equivalence conjecture\", \"statement\": \"Let $G$ be a graph and $k$ a positive integer. A **$k$-flow** is a nowhere-zero integer flow with $0<|f(e)|<k$ on every edge, and an **$A$-flow** is a nowhere-zero flow with values in an abelian group $A$. Let $\\\\mathcal{F}(G,k)$ and $\\\\mathcal{F}(G,\\\\mathbb{Z}_k)$ be the reconfiguration graphs whose vertices are the corresponding flows and whose edges represent flow-adjacency.\\n\\n**Esperet et al.'s flow reconfiguration conjecture.** For each graph $G$ and each positive integer $k$,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\mathcal{F}(G,k)\\\\text{ is connected if and only if }\\\\mathcal{F}(G,\\\\mathbb{Z}_k)\\\\text{ is connected}.\\n$$\\n\\nOne direction is easy, since reducing flow values modulo $k$ maps walks to walks. The reverse direction remains open; the source also gives examples showing that reconfiguration can distinguish nonisomorphic groups of the same order.\", \"statement_completeness\": \"full\", \"post_type\": \"conjecture\", \"status\": \"open\", \"tags\": [\"graph-reconfiguration\", \"graph-theory\", \"nowhere-zero-flows\"], \"importance\": \"corpus\", \"source_name\": \"Daniel W. Cranston, Jiaao Li, Bo Su, Zhouningxin Wang and Ningyan Xu, \u201cReconfiguration of Nowhere-zero Flows\u201d, arXiv:2606.24685 (2026).\", \"source_url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.24685\", \"first_stated_year\": 2026, \"first_stated_year_source_url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.24685\", \"documented_by_year\": null, \"documented_by_source_url\": null, \"references\": \"Source: https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.24685\\n\\nStatus: **open** according to the source (as of June 2026). \u201cDespite some beautiful partial results , all $3$ conjectures remain open.\u201d\", \"solutions\": [], \"solution_count\": 0, \"has_formal_statement\": null, \"has_bounty\": null, \"created_at\": \"2026-08-11T05:41:34.754172Z\", \"edited_at\": null, \"lastmod\": \"2026-09-20T16:36:30Z\", \"in_sitemap\": true, \"historical\": false, \"retrieval_source\": \"probxiv_2026-09-29\"}\n"
  },
